  "query_preview": "..\nSome lingering low clouds this morning, but that will thin more\nby this afternoon. After a bit of a chilly start, especially \nfor locales that clear south and east of Tucson, highs in the\n70s for lower deserts are expected. Slightly cooler for higher\nvalley locations south and east of Tucson. Mtns will be in the\n40s/50s. \n\nTemps warm a bit more on Monday with highs in the middle and\nupper 70s lower deserts and lower 70s higher valleys. Mtns in\nthe 50s. Similar conditions continue into Monday as weak mid\nlevel ridging pushes east as the next upper level trof\napproaches the region Monday night. Over the past couple\nforecast cycles, guidances has gradually pulled back on rain\nchances Tue-Wed, with the best chance north of the area.\nRegardless, at least some showers and gusty winds are expected \nas the system passes through. \n\nAfter a few dry days, another system is possible by next\nweekend. Confidence remains low as the system could largely stay\nnorth of the region.",
